<section>
	<h2 id="demo-content">Demo Content</h2>
	<p>Before importing, go to <strong>Appearance &gt; Install Plugins</strong> and install and activate <strong>One Click Demo Import</strong>, the other required plugins and the plugins used by your chosen demo, then complete <a href="#updates">theme registration</a>. The import skips demo content whose plugin isn't active. The demo projects need <strong>Portfolio Post Type</strong>, the contact forms need <strong>Contact Form 7</strong> and the shop products need <strong>WooCommerce</strong>. These plugins are only recommended and the importer doesn't install them, so activate them first if you want those parts of the demo.</p>
	<h3 id="one-click-demo-install">One Click Demo Install</h3>
	<p>
		You can import demo content from our demo site (with blurred licensed images) in two clicks.
	</p>
	<div class="warning">
		Don't forget to activate all required plugins before importing demo data.
	</div>
	<p>
		Go to <kbd><kbd><samp>wp-admin</samp></kbd>&nbsp;→ <kbd><samp>Appearance</samp></kbd>&nbsp;→ <kbd><samp>Import Demo Data</samp></kbd></kbd>. Here, you can select which demo data you want to import. First, choose from one of our four demo pages:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>BuildPress Classic</li>
		<li>BuildPress Light</li>
		<li>BuildPress Landscape</li>
		<li>BuildPress RTL</li>
	</ul>
	<p>Then, hover over the demo and choose whether you want to import the SiteOrigin or Elementor version by clicking its logo under <strong>Choose page builder</strong>.</p>
	<p>
		Finally, check the plugins the demo needs and click the <kbd>Continue &amp; Import</kbd> button to begin the import process. Your site should be ready after a few minutes.
	</p>

	<h3 id="elementor-demos">Elementor Demos</h3>
	<p>
		The Elementor versions of the demos are built differently from the SiteOrigin versions, so some sections of these docs don't apply to them:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>The header and footer are the <strong>Header</strong> and <strong>Footer</strong> templates of the Elementor Header &amp; Footer Builder plugin (shown as <strong>Ultimate Addons for Elementor</strong> on the Plugins screen). They replace the theme's header and footer on every page, so the logo, top bar, header widgets, footer widgets and footer text settings described in the <a href="#header">Header</a> and <a href="#footer">Footer</a> sections don't change your site. Edit the templates with Elementor in <strong>UAE &gt; Header &amp; Footer</strong>.</li>
		<li>The front page slider is a <strong>Smart Slider 3</strong> slider. Edit it in the Smart Slider 3 plugin instead of the <a href="#slider">Front page slider</a> meta box.</li>
		<li>The pages, including the coming soon pages, are built with Elementor. Open a page and click <strong>Edit with Elementor</strong> to change it.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		One Click Demo Import also imports the Smart Slider 3 sliders and the Elementor global colors and fonts. A manual XML import doesn't, so use One Click Demo Import for the Elementor demos.
	</p>

	<h3 id="import-xml-file">Import XML File</h3>
	<p>
		If you want to import the demo content the old-fashioned way, you can get a fresh copy of the <strong>XML files</strong> on our server at these URLs:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/xml-exports/buildpress-latest.xml">BuildPress Classic SiteOrigin</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/xml-exports/buildpress-light-latest.xml">BuildPress Light SiteOrigin</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/xml-exports/buildpress-landscape-latest.xml">BuildPress Landscape SiteOrigin</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/xml-exports/buildpress-rtl-latest.xml">BuildPress RTL SiteOrigin</a></li>
	</ul>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/xml-exports/buildpress-elementor-latest.xml">BuildPress Classic Elementor</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/xml-exports/buildpress-light-elementor-latest.xml">BuildPress Light Elementor</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/xml-exports/buildpress-landscape-elementor-latest.xml">BuildPress Landscape Elementor</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/xml-exports/buildpress-rtl-elementor-latest.xml">BuildPress RTL Elementor</a></li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Don’t forget to activate all required plugins before importing demo data. To import the demo data go to <kbd><kbd><samp>Tools</samp></kbd>&nbsp;→ <kbd><samp>Import</samp></kbd></kbd>, click on <kbd>WordPress</kbd> (install the <strong>WordPress Importer</strong> plugin if not already installed) and upload/import the previously saved xml file. Don’t forget to check the <kbd>Download and import file attachments</kbd> checkbox to also import the images.
	</p>
	<h4>Demo Widgets</h4>
	<p>
		After you import the demo content, you can also import widgets the old-fashioned way. The files for widget import are also located on our server:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/json-widgets/buildpress.json">BuildPress Classic SiteOrigin Widgets</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/json-widgets/buildpress-light.json">BuildPress Light SiteOrigin Widgets</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/json-widgets/buildpress-landscape.json">BuildPress Landscape SiteOrigin Widgets</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/json-widgets/buildpress-rtl.json">BuildPress RTL SiteOrigin Widgets</a></li>
	</ul>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/json-widgets/buildpress-elementor.json">BuildPress Classic Elementor Widgets</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/json-widgets/buildpress-light-elementor.json">BuildPress Light Elementor Widgets</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/json-widgets/buildpress-landscape-elementor.json">BuildPress Landscape Elementor Widgets</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/json-widgets/buildpress-rtl-elementor.json">BuildPress RTL Elementor Widgets</a></li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Rename this file to <code>widgets.wie</code> (note the file extension) and use it in the plugin <a href="https://wordpress.org/plugins/widget-importer-exporter/" target="_blank">Widget Importer &amp; Exporter</a>. Go to <kbd><kbd><samp>Tools</samp></kbd>&nbsp;→ <kbd><samp>Widget Importer &amp; Exporter</samp></kbd></kbd> and import the file.
	</p>
	<h4>Customizer Settings</h4>
	<p>
		The last thing you have to import are the customizer settings. The files for that can also be found on our server:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/customizer-exports/buildpress.dat">BuildPress Classic Customizer Settings</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/customizer-exports/buildpress-light.dat">BuildPress Light Customizer Settings</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/customizer-exports/buildpress-landscape.dat">BuildPress Landscape Customizer Settings</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/customizer-exports/buildpress-rtl.dat">BuildPress RTL Customizer Settings</a></li>
	</ul>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/customizer-exports/buildpress-elementor.dat">BuildPress Classic Elementor Customizer Settings</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/customizer-exports/buildpress-light-elementor.dat">BuildPress Light Elementor Customizer Settings</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/customizer-exports/buildpress-landscape-elementor.dat">BuildPress Landscape Elementor Customizer Settings</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://artifacts.proteusthemes.com/customizer-exports/buildpress-rtl-elementor.dat">BuildPress RTL Elementor Customizer Settings</a></li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Install and activate the <a href="https://wordpress.org/plugins/customizer-export-import/" target="_blank">Customizer Export/Import</a>. Go to <kbd><kbd><samp>Appearance</samp></kbd>&nbsp;→ <kbd><samp>Customize</samp></kbd>&nbsp;→ <kbd><samp>Export/Import</samp></kbd></kbd> and import the file. Also check the <kbd>Download and import image files?</kbd> checkbox to import pattern images.
	</p>

	<h4>Disabling the page builder you didn’t use</h4>
	<p>
		Because Elementor and SiteOrigin Page Builder conflict with each other somewhat, you should disable the plugin for the page builder you didn’t use.
	</p>
	<p>
		If you ran One Click Demo Import with a SiteOrigin Page Builder version, go to <kbd><kbd><samp>wp-admin</samp></kbd>&nbsp;→ <kbd><samp>Plugins</samp></kbd></kbd> and:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Deactivate the <samp>Elementor</samp> plugin.</li>
		<li>Deactivate the <samp>Ultimate Addons for Elementor (UAE)</samp> plugin, called Elementor Header &amp; Footer Builder in the theme's plugin list.</li>
		<li>Deactivate the <samp>ElementsKit Lite</samp> plugin.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		If you ran One Click Demo Import with an Elementor version, go to <kbd><kbd><samp>wp-admin</samp></kbd>&nbsp;→ <kbd><samp>Plugins</samp></kbd></kbd> and:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Deactivate the <samp>Page Builder by SiteOrigin</samp> plugin.</li>
	</ul>
	
	<h4>After import setup</h4>
	<p>
		After you have imported the demo data, widgets and customizer settings, you should also set these things up:
	</p>
	{% part "content-includes/demo-content/after-import-setup" %}
	<p>
		If, for some reason, these URLs are not available and you downloaded the theme from ThemeForest, you may want to download the <kbd>All files &amp; documentation</kbd> zip from ThemeForest and you will find these files in the <samp>extras</samp> folder.
	</p>
	<div class="warning">
		Don't forget to activate all required plugins before importing demo data.
	</div>
	{# After Demo Content #}
	{% part "content-includes/demo-content/after-demo-content" %}
</section>
